00:28:30.735 --> 00:28:32.554
because that's sort of that, like if there's a hierarchy

00:28:32.587 --> 00:28:34.394
of development, that one came first. So that's,

00:28:35.155 --> 00:28:35.300
um,

00:28:36.206 --> 00:28:38.939
with practice, that, that one is more accessible.

00:28:42.762 --> 00:28:45.353
But it's, but it all, but it's still, it's still

00:28:45.402 --> 00:28:46.593
a movement that takes

00:28:47.430 --> 00:28:52.021
postural control, motor planning, coordination, visual attention. The ability to

00:28:52.053 --> 00:28:52.839
initiate. So

00:28:53.577 --> 00:28:55.549
there's this misconception that pointing

00:28:56.367 --> 00:28:58.933
is really simple, but it's not.

00:28:59.975 --> 00:29:00.440
Oh, yeah.

00:29:01.274 --> 00:29:05.106
They're coordinating an incredibly complex sequence of motor tasks when

00:29:05.106 --> 00:29:06.998
they do that because you need—

00:29:07.993 --> 00:29:08.410
a lot of them

00:29:09.516 --> 00:29:12.034
