00:29:13.124 --> 00:29:15.562
almost all of our movement is initiated from the trunk

00:29:15.562 --> 00:29:18.063
and pelvis. So you need that postural control and stability.

00:29:18.576 --> 00:29:21.364
Otherwise, it's much harder to make precise movements. You need

00:29:21.396 --> 00:29:24.120
head control to orient yourselves to the, to the board

00:29:24.120 --> 00:29:27.085
or the, the, the screen or into your communication partner.

00:29:28.191 --> 00:29:34.184
And the eyepiece, there are almost all neurodevelopmental disorders have

00:29:34.312 --> 00:29:35.129
a component where

00:29:35.882 --> 00:29:36.571
there's visual,

00:29:37.485 --> 00:29:41.282
visual motor and ocular motor challenges. We have 12 cranial

00:29:41.282 --> 00:29:44.583
nerves. 4 of them alone are dedicated to the eyes.

00:29:44.631 --> 00:29:46.464
Wow. That's how important the eyes are. Oh,

00:29:47.445 --> 00:29:51.078
Ability to, to generate smooth, controlled movement.

00:29:53.056 --> 00:29:55.986
And it's interesting, just on that point with eye control,

00:29:56.115 --> 00:29:56.533
I know

00:29:58.063 --> 00:30:01.444
when you're talking about, again, nonspeakers and the inability to

00:30:01.444 --> 00:30:04.437
